<title>UK: Ford unit prices $1.0 billion 10-year bond.</title>
<headline>Ford unit prices $1.0 billion 10-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following global bond has been priced, joint lead managers Merrill Lynch and Morgan Stanley said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The deal was launched on Tuesday.  BORROWER   FORD MOTOR CREDIT CORP</p>
<p> AMT	  $1.0 BLN  COUPON     7.20	MATURITY    15.JUN.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.914    PAY DATE   *11.JUN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.45	REOFFER    99.914    SPREAD	+59 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	A1	  LISTING    LUX/SI/HK PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  A+	  DENOMS (K) ONE	 SALE LIMITS US/UK/SGP</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.15	SELL CONC  0.30	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.625 PCT U.S. T-NOTE DUE 15.MAY.07  NOTES     *LONG FIRST COUPON.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
